#-------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Statements the series adds whose dormancy rests on something other than a
# name the series introduces.
#
# unused_paths.py cannot decide these, because the argument is about what an
# existing name can hold rather than about a hook being NULL.  Each one is
# read by hand, recorded here with that reading, and printed on every run --
# a suppression nobody sees is worse than no check.
#
# Adding an entry is a review decision.  The question it has to answer is:
# on a server where no extension of this port is loaded, can control reach
# this statement?  If yes, it does not belong here; redesign the patch.
#
# Format:  <path> : <function> : <reason>
#

src/backend/access/transam/xact.c : EstimateTransactionStateSpace : The shortcut is
	guarded by "nParallelCurrentXids > 0 && !IsParallelWorker()".  In an
	unpatched server the only assignment that makes nParallelCurrentXids
	non-zero is in StartParallelWorkerTransaction(), which runs only in a
	parallel worker, so the second test is false wherever the first is true and
	the branch cannot be reached.  The other writer is XactAdoptCurrentXids(),
	which this series adds and which refuses to run in a parallel worker.
